From: K230 AMP development <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: k230: describe small-core AMP slot on CanMV-K230 V3 LCD

k230-canmv-v3-lcd.dts is a sibling of k230-canmv-v3.dts, not a child: both
include k230.dtsi directly, so the AMP carveout and the UART3 handover do not
propagate and have to be repeated here.

This matters on V3 because the LCD device tree is the board default -- it is
listed first in BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_INTREE_DTS_NAME, and post-image.sh symlinks
k.dtb to the first entry. Without this patch the AMP configuration has to boot
the non-LCD DTB to stay clear of the big core's memory, which leaves the panel
undescribed; with it, the default LCD DTB is safe to boot alongside the
big-core firmware.

--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230-canmv-v3-lcd.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230-canmv-v3-lcd.dts
@@ -27,6 +27,22 @@
 		reg = <0x0 0x0 0x0 0x40000000>;
 	};
 
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <2>;
+		#size-cells = <2>;
+		ranges;
+
+		big_core_firmware: big-core-firmware@1c000000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x1c000000 0x0 0x01000000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		amp_shared_memory: amp-shared-memory@1d000000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x1d000000 0x0 0x03000000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+	};
+
 	sound {
 		status                      = "okay";
 		compatible                  = "canaan,k230-audio-inno";
@@ -39,8 +55,9 @@
 &uart0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+/* UART3 is connected to CH342 channel B and belongs to big-core firmware. */
 &uart3 {
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 &mmc_sd1{
 	status = "okay";
